Subject: [PATCH 25/40] =?UTF-8?q?hottyterm:=20a=20HOTTY=20click=20carries?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20the=20platform's=20count=20(SPEC=20=C2=A79)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GTK's click gesture counts presses by the user's double-click time and
distance (n_press), which Ghostty ignored. gcMouseDown hands it to
hotty.surfaceClickCount, and the next press on a surface passes it to
hotty_host_pointer, which keeps the run to one element (hotty-blitz
13300e2). Where no count comes from the platform, as on macOS today,
hotty.zig counts presses as Ghostty's own selection does:
click-repeat-interval (the OS value on macOS) and a cell's width.
ensureHost turns counts on, so the caps report `count`.

Lines added outside tests: apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig 1 (1 changed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
